# trait_fold_reject.tkr — the §9.4 composition-fold REJECT channel. Two un-absorbable same-name
# method collisions live one per namespace under src/, and the single failing build (the fold walks
# every composer and names each) reports both. A fold error is a HARD pre-walk boundary, so these
# live apart from the checker-stage trait rejects.

Feature: trait_fold reject — the composition fold rejects un-absorbable collisions (§9.4)

  # (r7_two_traits_conflict) two composed traits provide `k` with differing bodies — no absorb.
  Scenario: r7_two_traits_conflict — two composed traits with differing bodies are rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "provided by composed traits with differing bodies"

  # (r8_host_redefine_conflict) the host redefines a composed trait's `k` with a different body.
  Scenario: r8_host_redefine_conflict — a host redefining a composed member differently is rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "redefines 'k' with a body different"
